# An upgrade to a kernel that crashes: the rollback brings the old kernel
# back, and the files are untouched. (`failboot` makes a kernel on trial panic.)
@sata
@blank-disk 64
@install-medium failboot
$& install sata0
> yes
$wait
Installed on sata0. Take out the install medium and type: reboot
@boot-disk
$ echo precious > /data/keep.txt
@boot-medium newer
$& install sata0
> yes
$wait
~ ^Kernel b\d+ is in slot b of sata0

# The new kernel panics on its trial boot; the next boot is the old one.
@boot-disk crash
~ ^\[slots\] trial of build b\d+ in slot b failed \(crashed or hung\); rolled back to slot a$
$ slots
booted slot: a
good slot:   a
~ failed
$ cat /data/keep.txt
precious

# After that the upgrade can be tried again.
@boot-medium newer
$ install
~ BeeCodersOs b\d+ \(boot, os, data\)
$& install sata0
> yes
$wait
~ ^Kernel b\d+ is in slot b of sata0
